[center][size=6][b]Better Flight[/b][/size]
[size=4]6DOF flight controls for No Man's Sky[/size][/center]

Strafe sideways. Thrust up and down. Stop dead in space. Turn without the ship banking on its own.

No Man's Sky ships only ever fly where the nose points. Better Flight gives you control over all six directions of movement - forward/back, left/right, up/down, pitch, yaw and roll - using a small native module that adds real thruster movement on top of a retuned flight model.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Strafe[/b] left and right, [b]thrust[/b] up and down
[*]Mouse turning no longer rolls the ship
[*]Ships can come to a complete stop
[*]Momentum carries - the ship doesn't snap to where the nose points
[*]Adjustable thruster strength, editable while playing
[*]F8 toggles strafe on and off
[/list]

[size=5][b]Controls[/b][/size]
[code]
W / S    thrust / brake            LShift  boost
A / D    STRAFE left / right       B       pulse jump   (was Space)
Space    THRUST UP                 N       land         (was E)
LCtrl    THRUST DOWN               F       exit / tag   (was E)
Q / E    roll                      C       scan
Mouse    pitch / yaw, no banking   F8      strafe on/off
[/code]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Windows[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Close the game.
[*]Extract the zip into your [i]No Man's Sky[/i] folder (the one containing [i]Binaries[/i] and [i]GAMEDATA[/i]) and merge folders.
[*]Launch normally.
[/list]
Manual install is recommended - part of the mod goes in [i]Binaries[/i], which mod managers don't always handle.

[b]Linux / Steam Deck[/b]
Install as above, then add this to the game's Steam launch options:
[code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="winmm=n,b" %command%[/code]
or run the included [i]linux_wine_override.py[/i] once with the game closed. Use exactly [b]n,b[/b] - plain [b]n[/b] breaks it.

[size=5][b]Please read[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Custom keybinds:[/b] if you've changed keys in the game's Controls menu, those override this mod's layout. Reset to default or set roll/pulse/land/exit by hand. Strafe works either way.
[*][b]Game updates:[/b] strafe usually survives updates, and switches itself off safely if it can't. The flight retune is tied to a game version and may need a mod update after a patch.
[*][b]Conflicts:[/b] other mods that replace [i]GCSPACESHIPGLOBALS.GLOBAL.MBIN[/i] (most flight/speed mods), keyboard binding mods, and other mods installed as [i]winmm.dll[/i].
[*][b]Keyboard only[/b] for now - controllers and HOTAS can't strafe yet.
[*]Typing A, D or Space in text chat while flying also strafes.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
Tested on Steam under Linux (Proton). Steam on Windows is expected to work - reports welcome. GOG untested. Xbox / Game Pass not supported.

[b]Antivirus:[/b] some antivirus tools flag unknown DLLs that hook into games. [i]winmm.dll[/i] only loads inside No Man's Sky, and forwards calls to Windows' own winmm.dll.

[size=5][b]Bug reports[/b][/size]
Set [i]Debug = 1[/i] in [i]Binaries/BetterFlight.ini[/i], reproduce the problem, and attach [i]Binaries/BetterFlight.log[/i]. It records whether the module loaded and why strafe didn't apply.

[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [i]Binaries/winmm.dll[/i], [i]Binaries/BetterFlight.ini[/i], [i]GAMEDATA/MODS/BetterFlight[/i] and [i]GAMEDATA/MODS/BetterFlightControls[/i]. On Linux, also remove the launch option.

